I read all of `flow-space-ui` (about 8,300 lines) and checked it against the earlier UI report, so nothing below repeats work that's already done. The type check passes, lint shows 5 warnings, and I measured a production build. I didn't open the app in a browser, because that needs a test login. Anything about how a screen looks is marked "to check".

The groundwork from the earlier sessions holds up: the safe expression evaluator, HTTPS and CSP, the cookie-based login refresh, the new-version notice and the smoke tests. What remains is mostly how the app handles data while it runs, plus two architecture habits that keep producing bugs.

## Top 5 by effect for the effort

| # | Finding | Why it matters | Effort |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | **One failed 60-second state poll blanks the diagram.** [dashboard-page-context.tsx:203](flow-space-ui/src/pages/dashboard-page/dashboard-page-context.tsx#L203) sets the states to `undefined` on any error, and [mnemoschema.tsx:103](flow-space-ui/src/pages/dashboard-page/components/mnemoschema/mnemoschema.tsx#L103) then shows "Нет данных". | A network glitch or a deployment empties the operator's screen for a minute and shows an error toast. Keeping the last values and marking them stale is the right behaviour for monitoring. | S |
| 2 | **Map marker colours never update.** They are fetched once when the map opens ([map-page.tsx:234](flow-space-ui/src/pages/map-page/map-page.tsx#L234)), while the side menu's alarms refresh every 10 s. | The overview map can show green while the menu shows red. | S–M |
| 3 | **Local-storage settings belong to the browser, not the user, and survive sign-out.** These are the alarm mutes ([emergency-mute-manager.ts:9](flow-space-ui/src/services/emergency-mute-manager.ts#L9)), the last opened page, report parameters and dialog sizes. Sign-out clears only the login ([auth-store.tsx:127](flow-space-ui/src/contexts/auth-store.tsx#L127)). | On a shared control-room PC, user B silently inherits A's "До устранения" mutes. B can also land on A's last device and get an error if B has no access to it. | S |
| 4 | **There is no error boundary anywhere.** The forms are built from the data schemas without checks, e.g. `dataschema.ui.groups.find(...).order` in [control-form.tsx:116](flow-space-ui/src/pages/dashboard-page/components/control/control-form.tsx#L116) and [map-page-popup-content.tsx:175](flow-space-ui/src/pages/map-page/map-page-popup-content.tsx#L175). | One mistake in a statics `data-schema.json` (a group id that isn't listed) leaves the whole app as a white screen. | S |
| 5 | **The graph and alarm-log dialogs load at sign-in.** Their libraries are 1.0 MiB of the 3.05 MiB start JavaScript. | Loading them only when opened, as the help dialog already does, should cut the start download by about 35 %. That is an estimate; it still needs a test build. | S |

## UX

- **"Нет данных" doubles as the loading state**, e.g. [dashboard-page.tsx:247](flow-space-ui/src/pages/dashboard-page/dashboard-page.tsx#L247) and [report-page.tsx:148](flow-space-ui/src/pages/report-page/report-page.tsx#L148). Every navigation flashes "no data" before the content arrives. A placeholder (like the map popup's) or a spinner should be used while loading, and "Нет данных" kept for real emptiness.
- **One full-screen loader for 14 kinds of request.** It is shown and hidden by editing the page directly ([shared-area.tsx:43](flow-space-ui/src/contexts/shared-area.tsx#L43)) and has no counter, so the first request to finish hides it while others are still running.
- **Freshness isn't visible.** Diagram values refresh every 60 s, alarms every 10 s, so a red alarm can sit next to normal-looking values for up to a minute. No "обновлено 12:03" is shown, and an open popover keeps the values it opened with.
- **Diagram view.**
  - The saved zoom is restored after 500 ms, so the diagram jumps ([use-mnemoschema-restore-transform-state.tsx:55](flow-space-ui/src/pages/dashboard-page/components/mnemoschema/use-mnemoschema-restore-transform-state.tsx#L55)).
  - Diagram heights are fixed per screen class, and large screens get 540 px against 640 px on medium ones ([use-mnemoschema-size.tsx](flow-space-ui/src/pages/dashboard-page/components/mnemoschema/use-mnemoschema-size.tsx)). To check on a big monitor whether space is wasted.
- **Sign-in.** The login box has no placeholder or label and no `autocomplete` hints for password managers ([signin-form.tsx:39](flow-space-ui/src/components/signin-form/signin-form.tsx#L39)). The "успешно выполнил вход" toast is noise.
- **Date ranges.**
  - Alarm log: only 1 h and "За текущие сутки", which actually means the last 24 h ([emergency-log-dialog.tsx:53](flow-space-ui/src/components/dialogs/emergency-log-dialog/emergency-log-dialog.tsx#L53)).
  - Graphs: day, week or month, one parameter at a time.
  - Neither offers a custom range.
- **Navigation.**
  - Every menu click waits 100 ms before navigating ([side-nav-outer-toolbar.tsx:75](flow-space-ui/src/layouts/side-nav-outer-toolbar/side-nav-outer-toolbar.tsx#L75)).
  - The menu finds the current item by polling the page every 100 ms, up to 11 times ([navigation.tsx:65](flow-space-ui/src/contexts/navigation.tsx#L65)).
- **Small text fixes.**
  - "Cирена" starts with a Latin C ([user-settings-dialog.tsx:82](flow-space-ui/src/components/dialogs/user-settings-dialog/user-settings-dialog.tsx#L82)).
  - The sign-out question ends with "!" ([shared-area.tsx:26](flow-space-ui/src/contexts/shared-area.tsx#L26)).
  - The menu label is `' Справка'`, with a leading space.
  - [index.html](flow-space-ui/index.html#L2) declares `lang="en"` for a Russian UI.
  - About still lacks the space before the version.
- **Accessibility.** There are 3 aria/role attributes in the whole app. Icon-only buttons (⋮, wide screen, close) have no tooltip, and the diagram works only with a mouse.

## Performance

These are the JavaScript files loaded at sign-in, measured from source maps with the new `.tools/bundle-size`:

| Source | kB | Used by |
|---|---|---|
| devextreme `ui` | 749 | Menus, TreeView, popups, forms |
| devextreme `grids` | 539 | **Alarm log only** (imported directly by [side-navigation-menu.tsx:13](flow-space-ui/src/components/side-navigation-menu/side-navigation-menu.tsx#L13)) |
| devextreme `viz` | 513 | **Graph dialog only** (imported directly by [dashboard-page.tsx:15](flow-space-ui/src/pages/dashboard-page/dashboard-page.tsx#L15) and the popover) |
| react-dom | 392 | |
| **Total** | **3,049 (874 gzip)** | |

- **The diagram is rebuilt from the SVG text on every poll.** That means parsing it, re-adding its stylesheet and re-creating its plug-in each time. Values are found with one search of the whole SVG per property ([use-mnemoschema-state-setup.tsx:108](flow-space-ui/src/pages/dashboard-page/components/mnemoschema/use-mnemoschema-state-setup.tsx#L108)). Parsing once, indexing the bound elements and updating only the values would make faster polling affordable.
- **Every dialog opening re-downloads the statics manifest uncached.** Each dialog creates its own data context, which fetches `manifest.json?v=<now>` ([use-flow-data.ts:289](flow-space-ui/src/contexts/app-data/flows/use-flow-data.ts#L289)). The help and JSON dialogs wait for that download.
- The 1.3 MB all-widgets theme stylesheet is still open from the earlier report.

## Reliability

- **Requests never time out.** The "не ответил … 10 сек." message is set ([use-auth-http-request.tsx:35](flow-space-ui/src/contexts/app-data/use-auth-http-request.tsx#L35)), but no timeout is. The fixed-interval polls can therefore pile up during an outage.
- **Some requests can't be cancelled.** In graphs and the alarm log, an old reply arriving late can replace newer data ([use-device-state-properties.tsx:10](flow-space-ui/src/components/dialogs/graph-dialog/use-device-state-properties.tsx#L10), [emergency-log-dialog-context.tsx:60](flow-space-ui/src/components/dialogs/emergency-log-dialog/emergency-log-dialog-context.tsx#L60)).
- **Diagram values are written as markup, not text** ([use-mnemoschema-state-setup.tsx:46](flow-space-ui/src/pages/dashboard-page/components/mnemoschema/use-mnemoschema-state-setup.tsx#L46)). This differs from the safe evaluator; it's low risk under the CSP, but the fix is one line per assignment.

## Architecture

State currently lives in four places:
- Zustand stores (login, settings).
- React contexts (app data, navigation, shared area, alarms, dashboard, each dialog).
- Module-level singletons (the mute manager, the dialog services).
- The page itself: alarm icons drawn into placeholders, the loader shown and hidden by style, the menu item found by searching the page.

The fourth produced #21 and the known "dead alarm icon after a mute" bug. Each proposal below removes more code than it adds:

1. **Alarm store with React icons.** The 10 s poll feeds a zustand store. The menu draws `<AlarmIcon deviceId>` itself, and the map and popover read the same store. This deletes the drawing code in [emergency-context.tsx:161](flow-space-ui/src/contexts/emergency-context.tsx#L161), the menu's change watcher and `toggleEmergencyIcon`. It fixes the dead click and finding 2.
2. **One dialog host instead of a separate app per dialog.** Today [root-dialog-service.tsx](flow-space-ui/src/components/dialogs/root-dialog-service.tsx) starts a separate React app for each dialog. A host inside the main app lets dialogs share the data, login and routing, which removes the manifest re-fetch and the loader z-index fixes.
3. **One data-fetching layer (recommended: TanStack Query, ~13 kB gzip).** It handles polling, cancellation, keeping the last data on error (finding 1), caching the manifest and schemas, and a loading flag per request. It replaces the "new random refreshToken to re-fetch" trick in 9 files, the hand-written `cancelled` flags and the global loader. Fixing each item separately without a new library also works, but it's more code to own.
4. **Menu selection driven by the route.** Select the menu item from the current address instead of polling the page and waiting on timeouts.
5. **A typed `DataSchema`.** Share one helper between the Параметры form and the map popup, which currently duplicate the group sorting. Many of the 116 `any` would then become checked.

## Maintainability

- **Unused, ready to remove:**
  - Files: `work-date-picker`, `work-date-widget`, `page-toolbar`, `main-context-menu`, `data-grid-icon-cell-value-container`, `custom-json-parser`, plus their models.
  - `use-quick-help-reference-data.tsx` (help now reads the statics).
  - Functions: `showConfirmDialog`/`Ex`, `showPromptDialog`, `getUuidV4`, `selectIsOperator`/`Guest`.
  - `isValidDeviceState` (#12) and the 70-line commented-out Ajv block.
  - `Footer`/`isShowFooter`.
  - 15 of the 17 custom translation strings (template leftovers about schedules and points). They are also re-registered on every render ([app.tsx:30](flow-space-ui/src/app.tsx#L30)).
  - Packages `ajv`, `@types/ajv` and `history`.
- **Hard-coded styling.** There are 127 inline style objects, the grey `rgb(118,118,118)` appears 8 times, and heights are set as `100vh − 50/77/150/210px`. The header is about 77 px tall, so the scroll area's −50 px looks wrong (to check), and `100vh` misbehaves on phones.
- **Duplication.** The graph and alarm-log dialogs repeat each other (date range, saved size, title menu), and the dashboard menu builders repeat too.
- **No unit tests.** `state-expression`, `data-helper`, `state-value-format` and the mute manager are pure functions and good Vitest candidates. The earlier 836-element diagram snapshot check could become a permanent test.

## Suggested order

1. **Small and safe:** remove the dead code, fix the texts, add an error boundary and a request timeout.
2. **UX:** keep the last values on a failed poll and show "обновлено"; separate loading from no data; store settings per user and clear them on sign-out.
3. **Performance:** load the graph and alarm-log dialogs on demand.
4. **Architecture:** the alarm store (which also fixes the map), the dialog host, then the data layer and updating the diagram in place.

